Usage: agent-deck session output [id|title] [options]

Get the last response from a session. If no ID is provided, auto-detects current session.

Options:

Output budget: default text output (also with --pane) strips ANSI escapes and is capped at
--max-tokens (default 25000, about 4 bytes per token). Longer output keeps its beginning and end
around an explicit "output omitted" seam and ends with the path of the full output retained on
disk. --json, -q/--quiet and --copy always carry the complete, unstripped source.

Change detection: --json carries content_version when the response is parsed from one
transcript file. Pass it back with --if-version to get {"unchanged":true} (no content, not a
logged read) while that file is unchanged; any change returns the full response and a new version.
